snapshot-menu (0.2.9) unstable; urgency=low

  * 06 Forensics & Response drops "Autopsy" (snapshot-autopsy.desktop).
    The vendor layer no longer ships Autopsy: it is Windows-first, its
    Linux build is a documented subset, and fitting it into an offline,
    read-only, quiet-on-the-wire image kept exposing new assumptions (a
    TSK JNI build, Java 21, pruned Tesseract data, a JRE module, an update
    check). The Sleuth Kit, TestDisk/PhotoRec and the field kit stay;
    analysis with Autopsy happens on a separate workstation after the
    field kit hand-off.

 -- Blackbird Cyber <snapshot@example.invalid>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:05:00 -0400

snapshot-menu (0.2.8) unstable; urgency=low

  * 03 Protocol Tools drops "pymodbus console"
    (snapshot-pymodbus-console.desktop). It ran pymodbus-console from the
    vendor layer, which stopped at start-up with "ImportError: cannot import
    name 'ModbusAsciiFramer' from 'pymodbus.transaction'": pymodbus-repl
    2.0.4, its last release (August 2024), only runs with pymodbus
    3.7.0-3.7.2, while the vendor layer pins pymodbus 3.11.3. The vendor
    layer no longer ships pymodbus-repl. mbpoll stays the interactive Modbus
    client, and the pymodbus library remains in the ICS Python shell.

 -- Blackbird Cyber <snapshot@example.invalid>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 17:32:25 -0400

